WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.030
Between 1901 and 2018, global
mean sea level rose 0.20 metres.

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.310
At first it rose 1.3 millimetres a year.

3
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.950
Then 1.9.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.950
From 2006 to 2018, 3.7.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.790
NASA satellites have measured
about 10 centimetres since 1993.

6
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.250
Where is all that extra water coming from?

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.750
More rain?

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.290
Floating Arctic sea ice?

9
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.200
Rivers carrying more sediment?

10
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.350
In this mission, you'll calculate
the rate of rise yourself,

11
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.390
and compare projections for 2100
under different emissions paths.

12
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.190
Then you'll follow emitted
carbon into the air,

13
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.970
the ocean and the land, and
see what it does to seawater.

14
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:48.120
Your mission: explain where the extra
water in the rising sea is coming from.
